rrdcached on FenrirOS
=====================

rrdtool ships rrdcached with a dinit service, /etc/dinit.d/rrdcached, that
is not enabled. It uses Debian's layout, which Proxmox VE (pmxcfs,
pvestatd) expects:

  databases  /var/lib/rrdcached/db       (created by tmpfiles.d)
  journal    /var/lib/rrdcached/journal  (created by tmpfiles.d)
  socket     /var/run/rrdcached.sock     (mode 0660, owner root)

It runs as root and listens only on the local socket (no network
listener). Start it, and enable it at boot if wanted:

  dinitctl start rrdcached
  dinitctl enable rrdcached

To change the options (write delay -w, jitter -z, a network listener -L,
another user), edit the command line in /etc/dinit.d/rrdcached; see
rrdcached(1).
